#
# Root filesystem profiles for the Raspberry Pi Pico.
#
# distrib/rp2040/mi.rp2040 brackets each optional feature between
# "#closure NAME" and "#endclosure NAME". A profile names the closures it
# keeps; distrib/rp2040/mkmanifest.py emits the base lines plus the lines
# of the named closures and refuses a composition whose hard links, parent
# directories or declared dependencies do not resolve. The Makefile
# variable PROFILE selects one, and its default is "full", which names
# every closure and reproduces the image the port ships.
# sys/arch/rp2040/doc/PROFILES.md is the authority for the scheme and
# carries the measured block cost of each closure.
#
# Grammar, one directive per line:
#
#   profile NAME [CLOSURE ...]          a selectable composition
#   closure NAME needs closure OTHER    OTHER must be selected too
#   closure NAME needs path PATH ...    PATH must reach the image
#
# A dependency is checked, never resolved: a profile that names a closure
# without the closure it needs fails the build rather than gaining the
# missing part silently, so the profile line stays the whole statement of
# what an image carries.
#

#
# Dependencies between closures.
#
# usr.bin/cc runs smlrc, as and ld over a source file and links the result
# against /usr/lib/crt0.o and /usr/lib/libc.a, so a compiler without the
# link library produces an a.out that no stage of the chain can finish.
# The requirement runs both ways: the library is 55 KiB of flash that
# nothing on the board reads once the compiler is gone.
#
closure toolchain needs closure toolchainlib
closure toolchainlib needs closure toolchain
closure toolchain needs path /usr/bin/cc /usr/bin/as /usr/bin/ld
closure toolchain needs path /usr/libexec/smlrc
closure toolchainlib needs path /usr/lib/libc.a /usr/lib/crt0.o

#
# usr.bin/pdp11 boots the pack named on its command line; /usr/v6/root.rk
# is the only pack the image carries, and /etc/menu's entry names it.
#
closure pdp11 needs closure v6disk
closure pdp11 needs path /usr/bin/pdp11
closure v6disk needs path /usr/v6/root.rk

#
# games/gamebox dispatches on argv[0]; fifteen, keen and bubble are hard
# links to it, and the manifest checker rejects a link whose source the
# profile dropped.
#
closure games needs path /usr/games/gamebox

#
# The compositions.
#
# base       the shell, /etc/rc, the multicall binaries and the editors
# benchmark  base plus CoreMark, for a reported score on a bare board
# developer  base plus the native compile chain and its link library
# games      base plus gamebox and its three entry points
# retro-lab  developer plus the PDP-11 emulator and its V6 pack
# full       every closure; the image the port ships
#
profile base
profile benchmark coremark
profile developer toolchain toolchainlib
profile games games
profile retro-lab pdp11 v6disk toolchain toolchainlib
profile full coremark pdp11 v6disk toolchain toolchainlib games
